{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.ConjPsdTraceOrthogonality","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.ConjPsdTraceOrthogonality","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Sort","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Set.Basic"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PSDTraceOrthogonality.psd_trace_orthogonality_holds_for_all_atoms","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PSDTraceOrthogonality.psd_trace_orthogonality_holds_for_all_atoms","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-psd-trace-orthogonality.lean#L109-L118","doc":"The conjecture statement: orthogonality holds for all atoms\nwith `A ≥ 2`.\n\nRef: [leitner2026] conj:psd-trace-orthogonality\n","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:psd-trace-orthogonality","label":"conj:psd-trace-orthogonality","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-psd-trace-orthogonality.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PSDTraceOrthogonality.PSDTraceOrthogonalityHolds.instances","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PSDTraceOrthogonality.PSDTraceOrthogonalityHolds.instances","kind":"def","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-psd-trace-orthogonality.lean#L107-L107","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PSDTraceOrthogonality.PSDTraceOrthogonalityHolds.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PSDTraceOrthogonality.PSDTraceOrthogonalityHolds.mk","kind":"ctor","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-psd-trace-orthogonality.lean#L106-L106","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PSDTraceOrthogonality.PSDTraceOrthogonalityHolds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PSDTraceOrthogonality.PSDTraceOrthogonalityHolds","kind":"class","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-psd-trace-orthogonality.lean#L98-L107","doc":"The orthogonality conjecture: an instance of\n`PSDTraceOrthogonalDecomp` exists for every atom number `A ≥ 2`.\n\nThis is the categorical statement of the empirical pattern; a\nproof would require Hecke representation theory at `q = q_0`\n(specifically, the seminormal-basis structure interacting with the\ncanonical `atom_braid_word_3A(Z, N)` word).\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PSDTraceOrthogonality.PSDTraceOrthogonalDecomp.etaSeparation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PSDTraceOrthogonality.PSDTraceOrthogonalDecomp.etaSeparation","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-psd-trace-orthogonality.lean#L96-L96","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PSDTraceOrthogonality.PSDTraceOrthogonalDecomp.etaLowerBound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PSDTraceOrthogonality.PSDTraceOrthogonalDecomp.etaLowerBound","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-psd-trace-orthogonality.lean#L95-L95","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PSDTraceOrthogonality.PSDTraceOrthogonalDecomp.psdFamilyAreTallNarrow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PSDTraceOrthogonality.PSDTraceOrthogonalDecomp.psdFamilyAreTallNarrow","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-psd-trace-orthogonality.lean#L93-L93","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PSDTraceOrthogonality.PSDTraceOrthogonalDecomp.traceFamilyAreLongString","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PSDTraceOrthogonality.PSDTraceOrthogonalDecomp.traceFamilyAreLongString","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-psd-trace-orthogonality.lean#L91-L91","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PSDTraceOrthogonality.PSDTraceOrthogonalDecomp.disjoint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PSDTraceOrthogonality.PSDTraceOrthogonalDecomp.disjoint","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-psd-trace-orthogonality.lean#L90-L90","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PSDTraceOrthogonality.PSDTraceOrthogonalDecomp.psdDominantFamily","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PSDTraceOrthogonality.PSDTraceOrthogonalDecomp.psdDominantFamily","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-psd-trace-orthogonality.lean#L89-L89","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PSDTraceOrthogonality.PSDTraceOrthogonalDecomp.traceDominantFamily","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PSDTraceOrthogonality.PSDTraceOrthogonalDecomp.traceDominantFamily","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-psd-trace-orthogonality.lean#L88-L88","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PSDTraceOrthogonality.PSDTraceOrthogonalDecomp.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PSDTraceOrthogonality.PSDTraceOrthogonalDecomp.mk","kind":"ctor","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-psd-trace-orthogonality.lean#L87-L87","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PSDTraceOrthogonality.PSDTraceOrthogonalDecomp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PSDTraceOrthogonality.PSDTraceOrthogonalDecomp","kind":"class","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-psd-trace-orthogonality.lean#L73-L96","doc":"**PSDTraceOrthogonalDecomp** — abstract class encoding the\nconjectured orthogonality of trace-dominance and PSD-dominance\nshape classes for an atom of mass number `A`.\n\nFields:\n\n- `traceDominantFamily` : the set of partitions of `3 * A` whose\n  `|y_λ|` is in the top decile.\n- `psdDominantFamily` : the set of partitions of `3 * A` whose\n  `ε_min(ρ_λ(T_w_sym))` is in the bottom decile (most negative).\n- `disjoint` : these two sets are disjoint.\n- `etaLowerBound` : the magnitude-separation function `η(A) := max\n  |y_trace| / |y_PSD|` is at least `10^(2A − 3)`.\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PSDTraceOrthogonality.Partition.isTallNarrow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PSDTraceOrthogonality.Partition.isTallNarrow","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-psd-trace-orthogonality.lean#L65-L71","doc":"The partition is **multi-row narrow** iff `numRows ≥ 3` and\n`maxRow ≤ 3 · numRows / |partition|` (heuristic; the empirical\nfalsifiers all have rows ≥ 4 and maxRow ≤ 5). The formal definition\nshould be the OPPOSITE of the long-string condition, plus a\nboundedness constraint on max-row. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PSDTraceOrthogonality.Partition.isLongString","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PSDTraceOrthogonality.Partition.isLongString","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-psd-trace-orthogonality.lean#L61-L63","doc":"The partition is **1- or 2-row** iff `numRows ≤ 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PSDTraceOrthogonality.Partition.maxRow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PSDTraceOrthogonality.Partition.maxRow","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-psd-trace-orthogonality.lean#L57-L59","doc":"The largest row (= max part) of a partition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PSDTraceOrthogonality.Partition.numRows","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PSDTraceOrthogonality.Partition.numRows","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-psd-trace-orthogonality.lean#L54-L55","doc":"The number of rows of a partition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PSDTraceOrthogonality.Partition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PSDTraceOrthogonality.Partition","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-psd-trace-orthogonality.lean#L49-L52","doc":"A **partition** of `n` represented as a non-increasing list of\npositive natural numbers summing to `n`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}